{
  "_comment": [
    "The shipped Lightspeed X-Series scenario. Every id is written by hand in an",
    "obviously sequential pattern so a reader can tell a seeded id from a minted",
    "one; the shapes are the vendor's, the values are not copies of any real",
    "account's. seed/constants.py names each of them and tests/unit/lightspeed/",
    "test_seed.py asserts the two agree.",
    "",
    "Two outlets and one register each: two rows make a list route's page",
    "boundary crossable, and two registers put the documented rate-limit quota at",
    "300 x 2 + 50 = 650 requests per five-minute window.",
    "",
    "Three payment types, one of them internal, because the payment_types:read",
    "scope is documented as 'excluding internal payment types' and a scenario",
    "with no internal type could not show that.",
    "",
    "No 'version' anywhere: the Lightspeed version is drawn from the retailer's",
    "one monotonically increasing counter at hydrate, in the order below.",
    "",
    "Slice L2b added 'sales' and the 'products' and 'customers' a sale must",
    "resolve against -- two products and one customer, the minimum. The sibling",
    "slice of the same issue owns those two collections and extends both lists",
    "with the rest of their documented members; these ids stay valid.",
    "",
    "Three sales, in the three shapes a till produces: one parked (saved and",
    "still editable), one closed with a card payment on the OPEN main register",
    "-- so the return action and the register payments summary both have",
    "something real to work on -- and one layby, which is a parked sale",
    "carrying the 'layby' attribute and a part payment, because the 2026-07",
    "schema has no LAYBY state (see machine.py).",
    "",
    "Money here is the wire's number (4.5), not the store's minor units:",
    "hydrate converts through model/money.py exactly as a request does.",
    "",
    "Every sale payment is dated inside the main register's open window",
    "(register_open_time 2026-09-01T08:00:00Z), so closing that register",
    "aggregates them into its closure's totals."
  ],
